remarks.para:
A request is eligible for retry only when all of the following are true:
(1) the HTTP method is not POST, or a POST carries an X-Idempotency-Key header;
(2) the number of retries already made is less than ;
(3) the failure is a retryable transport error, or the response status code is 409 (Conflict)
or >= 500 (server error).

member.summary:
Represents a Preference API response, which defines the checkout configuration
for Checkout Pro. A preference includes the items to purchase, payer information,
payment methods, shipping options, and redirect URLs.

member.param:
The value of the data.id query string parameter. Optional in the manifest:
if null, empty, or whitespace, the id: pair is omitted. When present,
the value is lowercased before being included in the manifest.
